{
  "_notes": [
    "SNES LoROM/HiROM flash cart. J1 (2x31 header) stands in for the 62-pin cart edge:",
    "SNES pin p (1..31, front row) -> J1 pin 2p-1 ; SNES pin p (32..62, back row) -> J1 pin 2(p-31), so opposite pins sit opposite.",
    "Cart edge used: 5/36 GND, 27/58 +5V, 6-18 A11-A23, 37-47 A10-A0, 20-23 D4-D7, 49-52 D0-D3, 24 /RD, 53 /WR, 48 /ROMSEL.",
    "Expansion pins 1-4/28-35/59-62, CIC 54-57, /IRQ 19, /RESET 25, SYSCLK 26 are left unconnected.",
    "Flash address A0-A18 = SNES A0-A18 (no mux). HiROM: 1MB native. LoROM: images are programmed at 64KB stride (32KB bank in the upper half of each 64KB) -> 512KB LoROM.",
    "Decode: U4 74HC00, U5 74HC32. N1=NAND(A14,A13). HIROM_TERM=OR(A22,N1). SW1 selects MODE_SEL = /ROMSEL (LoROM) or HIROM_TERM (HiROM).",
    "/SRAM_CE = OR(A15, MODE_SEL): LoROM -> banks 40-7D/C0-FF $0000-7FFF; HiROM -> banks 00-3F/80-BF $6000-7FFF.",
    "SRAM_SEL = NOT /SRAM_CE ; /FLASH_CE = OR(/ROMSEL, SRAM_SEL) ; /CE1 = OR(/FLASH_CE, A19) ; FLASH_SEL = NOT /FLASH_CE ; /CE2 = NAND(FLASH_SEL, A19).",
    "JP1 closed feeds /WR to the flash /WE for in-system programming; R1 pulls /WE high when the jumper is open."
  ],
